{"kind":"assert","text":"Codex: seven of stage two's twenty-one omission controls are now run by me rather than taken on the implementing agent's word. This one is the judgement call I flagged in the review request as mine rather than adopted, so it is the one I most wanted a red proof for.\n\nThe duplicate-head check deliberately ignores the checkout you cut from. Removing that exclusion, so raw head equality alone counts, fails four controls: TestCreatingACheckoutStampsItAndAllocatesOneAttempt, TestASecondCheckoutAtOneHeadIsWarnedAndTakesAFreshAttempt, TestTwoLinkedCheckoutsKeepTheirOwnRecordsAndAttempts and TestTheAttemptRefSurvivesCheckoutRemovalAndBranchDeletion. The mutant compiles and the worktree is back at a7360f6c clean.\n\nThat is the failure mode the exclusion exists to prevent, and the four reds show why it is not cosmetic: without it every branch cut from HEAD is a duplicate, so the confirmation flag would be required on ordinary creation, and a flag required always is a flag pasted in unread - which is exactly what adopted difference A10 exists to stop. Judge the reasoning on its merits; I am only reporting that the code is defended rather than asserted.\n\nThe seven now verified: destination containment inside this repository's Git directory, the configured checkout root refusal, the unreadable-projection degradation, the settled-lane confirmation, the foreign-genesis refusal, the create-against-missing allocation, and this duplicate-head exclusion. Fourteen remain on the agent's word and I am still not claiming them.","body":{"stale_bases":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:244249c09b5d8d6058d9be0307319054113ed75f stale; retired bases: git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:0169ac61d80658478db25ce500d46d087c06fdde, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:01c4e8b02601b3b35241c2baffd15e16e3e3d09d, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:033ceaa3c91aa563b1cc51c1b776c47c9